# Launcher build

`H&le.exe` in the repo root is how the app is opened. After any change under `ui/`, `shell/`, `engine/`, or `launcher/` that the launcher runs, do this before the work is finished:

1. Rebuild what changed.
   - Editor: `npm run build` in `ui/`, so `ui/dist` matches the source.
   - Window: `dotnet build shell/MacroShell.csproj -c Debug`.
2. The launcher starts `shell\bin\Debug\<TargetFramework>\MacroShell.exe`. It reads `<TargetFramework>` from `shell/MacroShell.csproj`.
3. If `launcher/` changed, republish the root exe from the repo root:

```
dotnet publish launcher/Vendetta.csproj -c Release -o launcher/publish
```

That publish copies `H&le.exe` to the repo root.
4. Include `H&le.exe` and the new `ui/dist` in the commit. Include the rebuilt `MacroShell.exe` when that file is tracked and the build changed it.

The launcher loads `ui/dist` through the shell exe. A source-only change leaves the app on the previous build.
